A||N||5||dgroves||Fuel pump won't start||||9||
Z||000000||dgroves||07-24-2001||02:16 PM||||I have an '86GT with 2.8L and auto tranny that had sat for probably 4 years before I got it.When the ignition key is turned on, the ECM is suposed to energize the fuel pump relay for about 2 sec. If the engine is cranked, the ECM sees a HEI signal and continues to run the pump. None of this happens! I have checked the green & white wire with a VOM and get 12V but no amperage (Won't light a 12V bulb) The relay will close if I apply 12V so it's OK. At this point I replaced the ECM but nothing changed. Thinking maybe the wireing was bad but it all checks out with a VOM. Not grounded, not open. The pump will run if you manually close the relay or apply 12V to the ALCL terminal "G". Seems very coincendental that two ECMs would have defects in the same driver. I inspected the boards and power transistors in the 1st ECM and found no evidence of heat or corrosion so if the driver is bad there isn't any obvious evidence showing. The oil pressure sender runs the fuel pump and the car starts and runs. The ECM sets no codes! Ogre, Oliver, Anybody.......At this point any advise would be appreciated.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Joe Torma||07-24-2001||02:37 PM||||Um, Try swapping the relay with the one next to it for the helluvit.  Check all the ground connections on the ecm.  ECM is probably shot.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||07-24-2001||04:06 PM||||hows about the oil pressure switch.I thought that the oil presure switch has to be working also for the fuel pump to work.||||reg||1
Z||000003||dgroves||07-24-2001||04:33 PM||||Fuel pump relay has been replaced. Swapping with A/C comp relay dosent do anything. Thanks anyhow Joe.<P>The schematics that I have show that the oil pressure sender works like an either/or deal. Both the O/P sender(Above 4 PSI)and the fuel pump relay, when energized by the ECM, will close the circuit to the fuel pump. The O/P sender is whats running the fuel pump now, not the fuel pump relay. Thanks Starfighter||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||07-24-2001||07:48 PM||||Do/have you checked for any fuel pressure?<BR>If you have none, try hot wiring the fuel direct to the battery as an operating check. No run? Bad pump.<P>Will the engine run with starting fluid?<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||dgroves||07-24-2001||08:36 PM||||Fuel pump runs!Produces adequate fuel pressure. Engine runs! OK? The fuel pump is running because the O/P sender is turning it on when the oil pressure rises above 4 PSI. It's supposed to be energized by the fuel pump relay vis a vis comand from the ECM.Thats what is not happening. The engine is running on the back up systen, not on the proper comand from the ECM. Does anybody know if there is a way to check the fuel pump driver in the ECM? Do I have two ECMs that have bad fuel pump drivers?||||reg||1
